  "final_text": "All four steps are done.\n\n1. The data view's time field is `timestamp`.\n2. I created the dashboard \"S4-2cdbd633 Flights\" with two panels: \"Flights over time\" (a line chart of flight count by `timestamp`) and a carrier panel (a bar chart of flight count by `Carrier`, top 10). I first gave the carrier panel a temporary title, \"Flights by carrier \u2013 temp\", which step 4 replaced.\n3. I created the rule \"S4-2cdbd633 Cancelled flights\" as an `.es-query` rule on `kibana_sample_data_flights`. It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 documents with `Cancelled: true` arrive in a 5-minute window. It was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n4. I renamed the carrier panel to \"Flights by carrier\". Reading the rule back shows it enabled, with status `ok`.\n\nI didn't re-read the dashboard after the rename, so the new title is confirmed only by the update succeeding.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
